# include/

Shared project headers. PlatformIO puts this directory on the include path, so
any source file can write `#include "header.h"` regardless of its own location.

## Files

### `header.h`

The umbrella header for the ESP32 firmware. It is included by `src/main.cpp`
and by every file under `src/web/`, and it pulls in:

| Group | Headers |
|---|---|
| Framework | `<Arduino.h>`, `<Wire.h>`, `<WiFi.h>`, `<ESPAsyncWebServer.h>` |
| Project libraries | `pulseSensor.h`, `pulseLEDSim.h`, `storage.h` |

Consequences worth knowing:

- Because it includes `WiFi.h` and `ESPAsyncWebServer.h`, anything that includes
  `header.h` only compiles for the `esp32` environment. The `uno` environment in
  `platformio.ini` cannot use it as-is.
- `lib/Display/display.h` is **not** included here. The I2C LCD code is dormant,
  so the LiquidCrystal_I2C dependency never enters the ESP32 build.
- `lib/Meter/` has no header yet — it is an empty placeholder, so there is
  nothing to add to `header.h`.

## Conventions

- Every header in this project uses `#pragma once` and contains declarations
  only. Definitions live in the matching `.cpp` in `lib/<Library>/` or
  `src/web/`.
- Library headers are included by bare filename (`#include "storage.h"`);
  PlatformIO's Library Dependency Finder resolves them from `lib/`.
- Headers local to one source folder (`src/web/server.h`, `src/web/handlers.h`)
  live beside their `.cpp` and are included with a relative name, not from
  here.
